  "worked_solution": "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\u27e8\\cdot ,\\cdot \u27e9$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016p(t)\u2016=\\sqrt{\u27e8p(t),p(t)\u27e9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=3-t+{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(-2)=9,\\,p(0)=3,\\,p(2)=5.\n$$\n\nComputing $\u2016p(t)\u2016$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016p(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{\u27e8p(t),p(t)\u27e9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(-2)p(-2)+p(0)p(0)+p(2)p(2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(-2)]^{2}+[p(0)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(9)^{2}+(3)^{2}+(5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81+9+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{115}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
